WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.056 --> 00:00:02.473
(rock music)

00:00:13.842 --> 00:00:14.675
- Hey, everyone.

00:00:14.675 --> 00:00:16.016
My name is Jesse from
the BuzzFeed food team

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:17.212
and today I'm gonna be cooking up

00:00:17.212 --> 00:00:19.193
four famous celebrity pancake recipes

00:00:19.193 --> 00:00:20.974
to see which one is actually the best.

00:00:20.974 --> 00:00:22.854
I have recipes lined
up from Gordon Ramsey,

00:00:22.854 --> 00:00:25.751
Ina Garten, Chrissy Teigen,
and for a little bit of fun,

00:00:25.751 --> 00:00:27.564
I even have a recipe from The Rock.

00:00:27.564 --> 00:00:28.947
I measure all the ingredients precisely

00:00:28.947 --> 00:00:30.183
to make everything fair.

00:00:30.183 --> 00:00:32.358
I picked my winner but I
got three of my friends

00:00:32.358 --> 00:00:34.358
to pick their winners
in a blind taste test

00:00:34.358 --> 00:00:36.123
to see which one is actually the best.

00:00:36.123 --> 00:00:37.532
So, let's get cooking.

00:00:37.532 --> 00:00:39.712
Gordon gets all fancy and
separates his egg whites

00:00:39.712 --> 00:00:41.974
from the yolks and whips them until foamy.

00:00:41.974 --> 00:00:43.699
This is just to incorporate
air into the pancakes

00:00:43.699 --> 00:00:44.970
to make them nice and fluffy.

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:46.410
And he must be cooking for a crowd,

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:48.637
because he used an entire liter of milk,

00:00:48.637 --> 00:00:52.277
eight teaspoons of baking
powder, and 640 grams of flour,

00:00:52.277 --> 00:00:54.888
which, if you're not familiar,
is a shit ton of flour.

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:56.871
After that, he mixes all
the remaining ingredients

00:00:56.871 --> 00:00:58.527
together in a separate bowl,

00:00:58.527 --> 00:01:00.435
he folds the whites back into that mixture

00:01:00.435 --> 00:01:01.977
and that batter is good to go.

00:01:01.977 --> 00:01:05.110
(upbeat pop music)

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:06.813
He cooks them in a buttered
skillet until browned

00:01:06.813 --> 00:01:08.430
but no lamb sauce this time.

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:11.413
(upbeat pop music)

00:01:11.413 --> 00:01:13.918
- I feel like these celebrities
have their coloration

00:01:13.918 --> 00:01:16.083
of pancakes down, pack.

00:01:16.083 --> 00:01:19.367
- A little thinner than I am used to.

00:01:19.367 --> 00:01:20.241
- Mmm.

00:01:20.241 --> 00:01:21.557
- They missed a few ingredients.

00:01:21.557 --> 00:01:22.390
- I love it!

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:23.223
It's like Sunday morning.

00:01:23.223 --> 00:01:24.353
- These are Gordon Ramsay's?

00:01:24.353 --> 00:01:27.805
I would expect any recipe of
his to be pretty top notch,

00:01:27.805 --> 00:01:30.552
and I have to say that these were.

00:01:30.552 --> 00:01:32.132
- [Jesse] Up next is Ina Garten's recipe

00:01:32.132 --> 00:01:34.139
for Banana Sour Cream Pancakes.

00:01:34.139 --> 00:01:36.449
She starts by sifting all
her dry ingredients together

00:01:36.449 --> 00:01:39.827
in one bowl and mixes all her
wet ingredients in another.

00:01:39.827 --> 00:01:42.778
This includes eggs,
lemon zest, good vanilla,

00:01:42.778 --> 00:01:46.010
her secret ingredient,
sour cream, then milk.

00:01:46.010 --> 00:01:48.393
She stirs that until
smooth then adds that back

00:01:48.393 --> 00:01:51.323
into her dry mixture and
mixes that up until smooth.

00:01:51.323 --> 00:01:54.364
She heats up a skillet with
butter, adds the batter to that,

00:01:54.364 --> 00:01:58.711
and tops each pancake with one
tablespoon of diced bananas.

00:01:58.711 --> 00:02:02.200
Flip 'em, then serve them with
butter, even more bananas,

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:05.329
and garnish with maple syrup.

00:02:05.329 --> 00:02:09.002
- Ohh, these look like
Instagramable brunch pancakes,

00:02:09.002 --> 00:02:11.169
that you pay like $20 for.

00:02:12.967 --> 00:02:16.025
- Mmm, never had banana pancakes before

00:02:16.025 --> 00:02:18.687
but this tastes like banana
pudding for breakfast.

00:02:18.687 --> 00:02:19.586
- But it's like nah.

00:02:19.586 --> 00:02:22.013
- The banana provides
an interesting contrast

00:02:22.013 --> 00:02:24.730
in taste and texture which is really nice.

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:27.647
- Whoever made this is heaven sent.

00:02:29.027 --> 00:02:32.874
- I'm so disappointed in myself,
I wish I liked this more.

00:02:32.874 --> 00:02:34.451
- [Jesse] Up next is Chrissy Teigen

00:02:34.451 --> 00:02:36.504
with a recipe for her Dutch Baby Pancake.

00:02:36.504 --> 00:02:38.609
Chrissy goes super simple
and just dumps everything

00:02:38.609 --> 00:02:40.792
straight into a blender
to make her batter.

00:02:40.792 --> 00:02:42.031
She blends it up until smooth

00:02:42.031 --> 00:02:44.622
and then dumps it directly into
a heated, cast iron skillet

00:02:44.622 --> 00:02:46.118
with two tablespoons of butter.

00:02:46.118 --> 00:02:47.230
She transfers that to an oven,

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:48.966
let's it bake for about 17 minutes,

00:02:48.966 --> 00:02:50.340
and it comes out looking like this

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:52.174
crazy, crackly weird looking thing

00:02:52.174 --> 00:02:54.755
and she finishes it with
butter, maple syrup,

00:02:54.755 --> 00:02:56.470
and a generous dousing of powdered sugar.

00:02:56.470 --> 00:02:58.516
So, Chrissy must have a sweet tooth.

00:02:58.516 --> 00:03:00.167
- It looks kind of like an elephant ear.

00:03:00.167 --> 00:03:01.097
- If you look at it,

00:03:01.097 --> 00:03:04.487
it looks like almost like
gelatinous in the middle.

00:03:04.487 --> 00:03:06.228
- This is like a french toast pancake.

00:03:06.228 --> 00:03:07.807
- You can taste a lot of egg in it,

00:03:07.807 --> 00:03:09.166
which I'm not used to in pancakes,

00:03:09.166 --> 00:03:10.152
it's not necessarily a bad thing,

00:03:10.152 --> 00:03:11.441
it's just really different.

00:03:11.441 --> 00:03:13.012
This is Chrissy Teigen, okay.

00:03:13.012 --> 00:03:15.035
- I like it, I love it.

00:03:15.035 --> 00:03:15.995
- [Jesse] Dwayne The Rock Johnson

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:17.794
uses traditional pancake mix.

00:03:17.794 --> 00:03:19.198
He posted his video on Instagram

00:03:19.198 --> 00:03:21.677
so I tried to mimic it
as closely as possible.

00:03:21.677 --> 00:03:24.153
He adds milk chocolate
chips, not semi-sweet,

00:03:24.153 --> 00:03:25.650
as he explained that sweet chocolate

00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:27.910
was his nickname at University of Miami.

00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:30.218
He cooks them on a stove top, flips 'em,

00:03:30.218 --> 00:03:32.756
and, as if chocolate
isn't enough for this guy,

00:03:32.756 --> 00:03:35.547
he finishes them with maple
syrup and whipped cream.

00:03:35.547 --> 00:03:37.745
This would certainly make
the perfect cheat day meal.

00:03:37.745 --> 00:03:41.724
- So these look like
IHOP birthday pancakes.

00:03:41.724 --> 00:03:43.100
- This is really good.

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:43.933
- This is it.

00:03:43.933 --> 00:03:44.766
This is the shit.

00:03:44.766 --> 00:03:45.599
This is my jam.

00:03:45.599 --> 00:03:48.189
The chocolate chips are like
super gooey on the inside,

00:03:48.189 --> 00:03:50.859
the dough is perfect, it's not too eggy.

00:03:50.859 --> 00:03:52.351
- These are The Rock's pancakes.

00:03:52.351 --> 00:03:54.176
I smell what The Rock is cooking.

00:03:54.176 --> 00:03:55.783
- I'm so ashamed!

00:03:55.783 --> 00:03:56.938
(laughing loudly)

00:03:56.938 --> 00:03:58.669
Whatever, I have low
brow taste I admit it.

00:03:58.669 --> 00:04:00.870
(hard rock music)

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:04.123
My favorite celebrity
pancake recipe is The Rock's,

00:04:04.123 --> 00:04:07.376
and, honestly, it's because
his has chocolate chips,

00:04:07.376 --> 00:04:08.209
that's it.

00:04:08.209 --> 00:04:10.592
- I would say my favorite of
the celebrity pancake recipes

00:04:10.592 --> 00:04:12.048
was Ina Garten's.

00:04:12.048 --> 00:04:15.342
Her's had a really great
taste with the bananas

00:04:15.342 --> 00:04:17.948
and also the bananas in
the pancakes themselves

00:04:17.948 --> 00:04:20.473
provided a nice change in texture.

00:04:20.473 --> 00:04:24.148
- My favorite celebrity
recipe is definitely The Rock,

00:04:24.148 --> 00:04:25.855
I mean, I don't know
how this fluffy monster

00:04:25.855 --> 00:04:27.684
made this beautiful combination,

00:04:27.684 --> 00:04:30.653
but I think it has the
right amount of chocolate,

00:04:30.653 --> 00:04:32.057
it has the right amount of pancake,

00:04:32.057 --> 00:04:33.619
and it has the right amount of sweetness,

00:04:33.619 --> 00:04:36.029
and it's still fluffy which is dope.

00:04:36.029 --> 00:04:38.208
(victorious music)

00:04:38.208 --> 00:04:39.155
- [Jesse] So, it turns out,

00:04:39.155 --> 00:04:41.791
The Rock has the best
celebrity pancake recipe.

00:04:41.791 --> 00:04:42.959
(loudly burps)

00:04:42.959 --> 00:04:45.285
- So sorry, so sorry.

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:47.789
Damn, those pancakes were good!

00:04:47.789 --> 00:04:49.529
- [Jesse] Which celebrity
recipe do you want to see next?

00:04:49.529 --> 00:04:51.453
Let us know in the comments below.

00:04:51.453 --> 00:04:54.084
(energetic music)

